column3:
The CLAD100 Aluminum Cladding System is an architectural-grade tongue-and-groove (T&amp;G) aluminum panel system engineered for seamless installation, modern aesthetics, and long-term durability. Featuring a fully enclosed interlocking profile, CLAD100 panels click securely into one another, creating a clean, continuous surface with no visible gaps.
Designed with a 4″ architectural design look, CLAD100 delivers a bold, linear appearance while maintaining a slim, lightweight aluminum profile. The system requires no mounting track, reducing installation complexity, labor time, and overall project cost.
Manufactured from 6063-T6 architectural-grade aluminum, CLAD100 is suitable for walls, ceilings, façades, and fence applications, for both interior and exterior use, including coastal and high-humidity environments.
<p>Premium aluminum cladding with a tongue-and-groove design, built for durability, style, and easy installation. The CLAD100 White Oak cladding system delivers a clean, modern finish for a wide range of applications.</p>
<h2>Introduction</h2>
<p>The CLAD100 White Oak aluminum cladding system is designed to transform walls, ceilings, façades, and fences with a refined, modern appearance. It combines the natural look of white oak wood with the strength and durability of aluminum.</p>
<p>Manufactured from high-quality aluminum, the system offers long-term performance while maintaining a clean, architectural finish. The realistic woodgrain surface delivers the warmth of natural wood without the maintenance challenges.</p>
<p>The tongue-and-groove design allows each panel to connect seamlessly, creating a smooth surface with no visible gaps. This makes the system suitable for both interior and exterior applications across residential and commercial projects.</p>
<h2>Benefits</h2>
<p>The CLAD100 White Oak cladding system provides a balance of performance, aesthetics, and efficiency.</p>
<p>The seamless tongue-and-groove design creates a smooth, modern appearance that enhances any space.</p>
<p>Constructed from aluminum, the panels are resistant to rust, corrosion, and long-term environmental wear.</p>
<p>The protective finish helps withstand sun exposure, rain, and humidity without fading or deteriorating like traditional wood.</p>
<p>The system is low maintenance and does not require painting, staining, or sealing—only occasional cleaning.</p>
<p>Lightweight construction makes the panels easy to handle and install while maintaining strong structural integrity.</p>
<p>The system is versatile and can be installed on walls, ceilings, façades, and fences in both vertical and horizontal layouts.</p>
<p>Aluminum is a non-combustible material, making it a safer alternative to wood cladding.</p>
<p>The trackless installation system helps reduce labor time and overall installation costs.</p>
<h2>How to Install</h2>
<p>Installing the CLAD100 White Oak cladding system is efficient and straightforward.</p>
<p>Begin by preparing the surface, ensuring it is clean, dry, and level. Depending on the application, a framing system may be required.</p>
<p>Measure the installation area and plan the panel layout, including direction and alignment.</p>
<p>Install the first panel and secure it using appropriate fasteners, making sure it is perfectly level.</p>
<p>Continue installation by sliding each panel into the tongue-and-groove connection of the previous panel, ensuring a tight and secure fit.</p>
<p>Repeat the process until the entire surface is covered, maintaining alignment throughout.</p>
<p>Finish by trimming edges if necessary and installing any required finishing trims for a clean result.</p>
<p>Always verify that all panels are properly aligned and securely fastened.</p>
<h2>Why Choose Our Product</h2>
<p>The CLAD100 White Oak aluminum cladding system is engineered for long-term durability and modern design.</p>
<p>Its aluminum construction provides superior strength compared to traditional wood or PVC cladding, eliminating issues such as warping, rotting, or excessive maintenance.</p>
<p>The seamless tongue-and-groove system ensures a clean, professional finish while simplifying installation.</p>
<p>The system is designed for efficiency, with no track required, saving both time and labor during installation.</p>
<p>The White Oak finish delivers a warm, natural aesthetic that complements a wide range of architectural styles.</p>
<p>It is built to perform in demanding environments, including coastal and high-humidity conditions.</p>
<p>Whether for residential or commercial use, the CLAD100 system offers a reliable, low-maintenance solution that enhances both appearance and performance.</p>		
  <style>
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }
    .grid-wrapper {
      max-width: 100%;
      margin: 0 auto;
      height: 90vh; /* adjust overall height */
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr 1fr;  /* big left, two right columns */
      grid-template-rows: repeat(3, 1fr);  /* 3 rows */
      gap: 10px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .grid-item {
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .grid-item img {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
      display: block;
      filter: brightness(0.85);
      transition: transform 0.4s ease, filter 0.4s ease;
    }
    .grid-item:hover img {
      transform: scale(1.03);
      filter: brightness(1);
    }
    /* layout spans */
    .item-large {
      grid-row: 1 / span 3; /* tall on the left */
      grid-column: 1 / 2;
    }
    .item-2 { grid-row: 1 / 2; grid-column: 2 / 3; }
    .item-3 { grid-row: 2 / 3; grid-column: 2 / 3; }
    .item-4 { grid-row: 3 / 4; grid-column: 2 / 3; }
    .item-5 { grid-row: 1 / 2; grid-column: 3 / 4; }
    .item-6 { grid-row: 2 / 4; grid-column: 3 / 4; } /* tall on bottom-right */
    /* Optional tiny text in corners like in screenshot */
    .grid-label {
      position: absolute;
      bottom: 10px;
      left: 10px;
      font-size: 30px;
      color: #fff;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      opacity: 0.85;
    }
    .grid-labelz {
      position: absolute;
      bottom: 10px;
      left: 10px;
      font-size: 50px;
      color: #fff;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      opacity: 0.85;
    }
/* Tablets and small laptops */
@media (max-width: 1024px) {
  .grid-wrapper {
    height: 70vh; /* shrink overall layout */
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .grid-label {
    font-size: 22px;
  }
}
/* Small mobile */
@media (max-width: 620px) {
  .grid-wrapper {
    height: 25vh;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .grid-label {
    font-size: 12px;
          position: absolute;
      bottom: 5px;
      left: 4px;
      color: #fff;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      opacity: 0.85;
      line-height: 1.5;
  }
    .grid-labelz {
    font-size: 14px;
  }
}
/* Small mobile */
@media (max-width: 620px) {
  .grid-wrapper {
    /* keep grid, just change layout */
    height: auto;
    gap: 2px;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;         /* 2 columns */
    grid-template-rows: repeat(4, auto);    /* 4 rows total */
  }
  /* Row 1: item-large full width */
  .item-large {
    grid-column: 1 / 3;   /* span both columns */
    grid-row: 1 / 2;
  }
  /* Row 2: item-2 | item-5 */
  .item-2 {
    grid-column: 1 / 2;
    grid-row: 2 / 3;
  }
  .item-5 {
    grid-column: 2 / 3;
    grid-row: 2 / 3;
  }
  /* Row 3 + 4: left column stacked, right tall item-6 */
  .item-3 {
    grid-column: 1 / 2;
    grid-row: 3 / 4;
  }
  .item-4 {
    grid-column: 1 / 2;
    grid-row: 4 / 5;
  }
  .item-6 {
    grid-column: 2 / 3;
    grid-row: 3 / 5;      /* spans rows 3 and 4 */
  }
}
  </style>
